2025-05-01 03:44:20 - Thread-1609 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "APP_GROUP_ID": identifies the app group – a required grouping column.  
• "USER_ID": identifies an individual Braze user – used to count unique users.  
• "SF_CREATED_AT": TIMESTAMP when the session‑start event row was written – easiest column for calendar‑day filtering (2023‑06‑01 → 2023‑06‑07).  
• "TIME": UNIX epoch seconds of the event – alternative time reference.  
• "SESSION_ID": optional if you need to de‑duplicate sessions.  
• Other columns (e.g., "PLATFORM", "DEVICE_ID", "OS_VERSION") can be inspected for extra filters but are not strictly necessary for the requested metric.

Below are ten Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex).  
All column, database, schema and table names are wrapped in double quotes.  
Each query is capped with LIMIT 20 to keep result sets small.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick peek at raw rows in the view (no filters)
SELECT *
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct app‑group IDs present in the table
SELECT DISTINCT "APP_GROUP_ID"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show all distinct calendar days (UTC) present inside June 2023
SELECT DISTINCT DATE_TRUNC('DAY', "SF_CREATED_AT") AS "SESSION_DAY"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'        -- inclusive
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'        -- exclusive upper‐bound
ORDER BY "SESSION_DAY"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Sample rows only for the requested June 1–7 window
SELECT *
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Distinct user IDs observed between June 1 and June 7
SELECT DISTINCT "USER_ID"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Count of rows (sessions) by app‑group and day for the window
SELECT
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  DATE_TRUNC('DAY', "SF_CREATED_AT") AS "SESSION_DAY",
  COUNT(*) AS "SESSION_ROW_CNT"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 2,1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Distinct platforms used in sessions during the requested week
SELECT DISTINCT "PLATFORM"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Device models for sessions started on June 3 2023
SELECT DISTINCT "DEVICE_MODEL"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE DATE_TRUNC('DAY', "SF_CREATED_AT") = '2023-06-03'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Count how many sessions each user opened per day (June 1–7)
SELECT
  "USER_ID",
  DATE_TRUNC('DAY', "SF_CREATED_AT") AS "SESSION_DAY",
  COUNT(*) AS "SESSION_CNT"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 2,3 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final metric – unique users who started a session
-- each day per app group between June 1 and June 7 2023
SELECT
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  DATE_TRUNC('DAY', "SF_CREATED_AT") AS "SESSION_DAY",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "USER_ID") AS "UNIQUE_USERS_STARTING_SESSION"
FROM "BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET"."PUBLIC"."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" >= '2023-06-01'
  AND "SF_CREATED_AT" <  '2023-06-08'
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 2,1
LIMIT 20;
```

